  "title": "The King's Letters of Seoul",
  "tagline": "READ THE NEW LETTERS",
  "plannedCases": 12,
  "mainMystery": {
    "truth": "Bun-i, the water-carrier who wrote the first letter in the new letters (Case 01), kept a small letter box. For five hundred years her family kept it: in every hard time a keeper wrote one short note in the King's letters, signed it with her water drop, and quietly helped. They never changed history; they kept the letters alive.",
    "culprit": "No one: the season's mystery is a family of keepers, not a crime; each case has its own small, made-up wrongdoer or puzzle.",
    "motive": "To keep the people's own letters alive, as Bun-i promised her teacher Sora.",
    "revealCase": "s5_ep08"
  },
